  <h2>Selected Projects</h2>

  <h3>Semra</h3>

  <p>A knowledge-discovery system built around a simple question:</p>

  <blockquote>How do we find what our documentation doesn't know?</blockquote>

  <p>
    Semra reverses the traditional RAG model by identifying information that
    falls outside the existing knowledge base instead of retrieving what is
    already documented. Using semantic distance analysis, statistical novelty
    detection, and agent-driven workflows, it automatically discovers
    documentation gaps, generates draft articles, and creates GitLab merge
    requests for human review.
  </p>

  <p>
    The platform combines vector search, multi-provider LLMs, production
    observability, durable job processing, evaluation frameworks, and workflow
    automation into a system designed to continuously improve organizational
    knowledge.
  </p>

  <h3>RagIT</h3>

  <p>
    An AI-powered literary analysis platform that transforms books into
    searchable knowledge systems using embeddings, vector search, retrieval
    pipelines, and narrative-aware exploration.
  </p>

  <h3>Arxiv Sanity Lite Modern</h3>

  <p>
    A modern resurrection of the classic research discovery platform, designed
    to help researchers and engineers navigate large collections of scientific
    literature.
  </p>

  <h3>Obsidian Remote Notes</h3>

  <p>
    A lightweight synchronization platform that extends personal knowledge
    management workflows beyond a single device.
  </p>

  <h3>Rustdrel</h3>

  <p>
    A terminal-based roguelike card game written in Rust, combining procedural
    gameplay, modular architecture, and classic command-line aesthetics.
  </p>

